    ("All Closed" / "<n> Open/Venting" / "—"), asNonEmptyString (length>0, untrimmed). JS truthiness for
    sentry/lock/homelink/guest reproduced incl. the web `latest?.sentryMode ?` quirk (any non-empty string,
    even "Off", renders Active). Verified by executed XCTest (30/30).
  Composition -> the six web GlassPanel cells, in web order: Lock (lock.fill/lock.open.fill, Locked/Unlocked)
    · Sentry (checkmark.shield/exclamationmark.shield, Active/Inactive) · Doors (door.left.hand.closed/open,
    Closed/raw doorState/Open) · Windows (recolored, All Closed/<n> Open/Venting/—) · HomeLink (house.fill,
    Nearby/Away) · Guest (person.fill.checkmark, Enabled/Disabled). Loading -> 6 skeleton blocks (web six
    <Skeleton height=120>); resolved grid wrapped in TSFadeIn(delay:0.1) (web FadeIn delay 0.1). An absent
    event renders the same six cards with the web optional-chaining fallbacks (Unlocked/Inactive/Closed/—/
    Away/Disabled) so the empty state is never a blank box.
  Shared components -> @/components/ui/GlassPanel -> TSGlassPanel; @/components/feedback/Skeleton ->
    TSSkeleton; @/components/motion/FadeIn -> TSFadeIn. Compiled against the REAL apps/apple component
